{"title":"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two distinct numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are chosen randomly from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/7/f47fe7039344156de1e719acdd24292420693c3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2, 2^2, 2^3, \\ldots, 2^{25}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"21\" />. What is the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4450ea731170407ac05f864e6b14b143319289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{a}b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> is an integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef87cb8609f1913833af8860927e8d6807635327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ \\frac{2}{25}\\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\frac{31}{300}\\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\frac{13}{100}\\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ \\frac{7}{50}\\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"419\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/c/1dc598816c276cd4112d3bbee57fdc4ad3456e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{a}b = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd7a6f3b9b5c19ce0f766d2716324d254d0b1cab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^z = b$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/8665647b23fab9e336680170ee5f300b4e8f4e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2^x$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42cd61f515c8d5dcddb4e58c05da64c76a411794.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2^y$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />; then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/8/3e84abb2639f6ef0729764fa6b26fed35652e64e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(2^x\\right)^z = 2^{xz}= 2^y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0a3b28bf9f18eee75137c1e4c733fcd8147cfdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\mid y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />. Here we can just make a table and count the number of values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> per value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. The largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and so we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/ddd06f47b860e56ff3baa39af4d951cec5a0a96e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{x=1}^{12} \\left\\lfloor\\frac{25}{x}-1\\right\\rfloor = 24 + 11 + 7 + 5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"543\" height=\"55\" />. \n</p><p>The total number of ways to pick two distinct numbers (where the order matters) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e777b3eabb07dad1b35ef2dba79d69063fd340ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25!}{(25-2)!}= 25 \\cdot 24 = 600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"197\" height=\"42\" />, so we get a probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/5/0356302d8fead7e95b073f1e162bcfc001d6380c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{62}{600} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{31}{300}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"133\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A\">2005 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160